---------------------------------------
The original Parallax Software Corporation code, including adaptations of
that code in this project, remains subject to the original Parallax terms
reproduced in LICENSES/LicenseRef-Parallax-Descent.txt. Those terms restrict
use to non-commercial, royalty- or revenue-free purposes.
Changing language, platform, filename, or implementation does not by itself
remove those terms. Preserve the original copyright and license notices.
No permission to use Parallax code for revenue-bearing purposes is granted
by dESPcent. Commercial permission must come from the relevant rights holder.
2. Independently authored dESPcent software
-----------------------------------------
To the extent the dESPcent authors hold the applicable rights, independently
authored dESPcent source code, build scripts, tests, and accompanying software
documentation are licensed under the MIT License in LICENSES/MIT.txt, unless
otherwise identified in the material or its accompanying notices.
This grant excludes Parallax code, adaptations of Parallax code, third-party
material, game assets, and the other excluded material described below. A
missing notice, lowercase filename, or location in a particular directory
does not establish independent authorship or erase an upstream license.
The MIT grant permits reuse of the covered independent material, including
commercial reuse. It does not authorize commercial use of the combined
Descent-derived firmware or override restrictions on other included material.
3. Third-party software
